:PNLGRP.
.*
:HELP name='ENDDBG/ALL'.
:IMHELP name=ENDDBG.
:EHELP.
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für den Befehl
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP NAME='ENDDBG'.
End Debug (ENDDBG) - Help
:P.
The End Debug (ENDDBG) command ends debug mode for a job, removes
all breakpoints and traces, clears any trace data, and removes all
programs from debug mode.  This command cannot be entered when one
or more of the programs in the call stack are stopped at a
breakpoint.  All breakpoints must be canceled by Resume Breakpoint
(RSMBKP) or End Request (ENDRQS) commands.  After this command has
been entered, all database files in production libraries can be
updated normally.
:P.
If ENDDBG is not done before the job has ended, all trace data is
printed.
:P.
:HP2.Restriction::EHP2. This command is valid only in debug mode.  To start
debug mode, refer to the STRDBG (Start Debug) command.
:P.
If you are servicing another job ENDDBG ends the service job
before it terminates debug mode.
:P.
There are no parameters for this command.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
:EPNLGRP.
